Package: livecaption
Title: Extract Windows Live Captions Text into R
Version: 0.1.8
Authors@R: 
    person(
        given = "Seyed Mahmood",
        family = "Taghavi Shahri",
        email = "mahmood.taghavi@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Description: Extracts text produced by Windows Live Captions and brings it into
    R for further processing, analysis, transformation, and export. Provides a
    small Windows-only interface for starting, stopping, and inspecting Live
    Captions, captures manually requested bookmarks with ISO 8601 timestamps,
    retrieves normalized overlap-aware text between numbered bookmarks, and
    supports immediate text capture relative to a stored baseline. This early
    release intentionally excludes continuous recording, subtitle, and Shiny
    functionality.
License: GPL (>= 3)
URL: https://github.com/Mahmood-Taghavi/livecaption
BugReports: https://github.com/Mahmood-Taghavi/livecaption/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports:
    jsonlite,
    processx
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Windows 11; Windows PowerShell 5.1 or later
